  "body_html": "<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"http://flowersinthebarrelofagun.files.wordpress.com/2012/02/siam1.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-444\" height=\"461\" src=\"http://flowersinthebarrelofagun.files.wordpress.com/2012/02/siam1.jpg\" title=\"siam1\" width=\"460\"/></a><a href=\"http://flowersinthebarrelofagun.files.wordpress.com/2012/02/20080912053830-lydia-lunch-queen-of-siam.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-443\" height=\"400\" src=\"http://flowersinthebarrelofagun.files.wordpress.com/2012/02/20080912053830-lydia-lunch-queen-of-siam.jpg\" title=\"20080912053830-lydia-lunch-queen-of-siam-\" width=\"400\"/></a></p>\n<p>Definitely Lydia Lunch’s best and most listenable work “Queen of Siam”, also her debut solo record, kicks straight in the balls. Queer lolita vocals, jazz, cabaret, avant-garde, depraved lyrics, dirty 80s guitars and sax, tension and tease… you got it all.</p>\n<p>How would I describe it with one word? BADASS.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>Here is my personal TOP 3 from this cult jewel. However, I recommend to enjoy it best in its full entirety:</p>\n<p>3: “Lady Scarface”</p>\n<p>[youtube http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UkGcTW4w4_o&amp;w=560&amp;h=315]</p>\n<p>2: “Spooky”</p>\n<p>[youtube http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SzQIvXQdJVQ&amp;w=560&amp;h=315]</p>\n<p>1: “Knives in the drain”</p>\n<p>[youtube http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tYeyVHOz950&amp;w=420&amp;h=315]</p>\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"http://flowersinthebarrelofagun.files.wordpress.com/2012/02/lidyalunch_2.jpg\"/></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>",
